{% aside type="caution" title="In development" %}
Model training for NAHPU is in early development. Commands, configuration
files, and model packages may change between releases.
{% /aside %}

NAHPU is adding deep learning (DL) features, such as identifying specimens
from measurements or photos. The models behind these features are trained and
fine-tuned with [milu](https://github.com/hhandika/milu), a command line tool
built on the `nahpu_dl` crate of the
[NAHPU API](https://github.com/nahpu/nahpu_api). Basic machine learning
methods, such as principal component analysis, live in the `nahpu_ml` crate.

## Current status

| Area                          | Status                                         |
| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| Tabular models (measurements) | Work end to end                                |
| Image models (specimen photos) | Work end to end                               |
| Text models                   | Planned                                        |
| ONNX import and export        | Planned                                        |
| Use inside the NAHPU app      | Planned; the app does not load models yet      |

## In this section

- [Architecture](/en/contributing/model-training/architecture/): how milu,
  `nahpu_dl`, and model packages fit together.
- [Fine-tuning](/en/contributing/model-training/fine-tuning/): train a new
  model or adapt a pretrained one to your data.
- [Guidelines](/en/contributing/model-training/guidelines/): set up the
  tools, prepare data, share models, and contribute code.

## Etymology

Like other NAHPU ecosystem tools named after deer and their close relatives,
milu is named after
[_Elaphurus davidianus_](https://www.mammaldiversity.org/taxon/1006318/), a
deer native to northeastern China.
